@startuml STM-8
!include _style.iuml
title STM-8 (System level) — Status of an RfidCard\nrfid_cards.status · v1.2 · 27/11/2026

[*] --> unlinked : Admin registers an online card\nwithout a Driver (UC-ADM-04)
[*] --> active : Admin registers a free_vend card,\nor an online card with a Driver
note left of unlinked
  A free_vend card never has a Driver:
  it is active from registration and only
  moves between active and blocked.
  The per-Charge-Point free-vend tag
  (UC-ADM-05) is not a card.
end note
unlinked --> active : Admin links it\nto a Driver
active --> unlinked : Admin unlinks it
active --> blocked : Admin blocks it\n(lost or misused)
unlinked --> blocked : Admin blocks it
blocked --> active : Admin unblocks it explicitly\n[online card: a Driver is linked; free_vend: no condition]
active -[dashed]-> blocked : «planned» account closure (UC-ACC-02, T162)\nlinked cards become blocked
note right of active
  Only active cards are accepted at the Charge Point.
  A session started offline with an unlinked or blocked
  card is still recorded, as unattributed (AD-6).
end note
note bottom of blocked
  Linking, relinking or unlinking never unblocks a card;
  only an explicit unblock does. There is no final state:
  a card is never deleted or retired.
  Blocking does not stop a running session; the block
  applies to the next Authorize and Start (BR-P23).
end note
@enduml
